  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Miniature workshop",
    "overview": "Warm timber, muted green paint, small buildings, and a jointed wooden visitor make the projects part of an explorable scene. Beveled pieces, screws, slats, grain, and restrained painted wear establish the miniature scale. The interface stays compact so the world remains visible.\n\nThis records the implemented home world and its HTML overlays. The existing standalone experience, resume, contact, privacy, and project routes retain their own templates; this file does not imply that they have been visually redesigned. The approved workshop direction is recorded in `PRODUCT.md`. Sources are `app/templates/home.html`, `app/static/css/world.css`, and `app/static/js/world/`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Real projects appear as inspectable objects with plain descriptive labels.",
      "Timber and painted geometry supply the visual detail; cream HTML panels support reading.",
      "Movement is visitor-controlled, and opening a panel preserves the current position.",
      "The project index and HTML fallback provide direct access to the same catalog."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Material Rule",
        "body": "Reuse the scene's generated wood and paint materials for new exhibits. Keep project-specific prop colors local to those objects.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shared Lettering Rule",
        "body": "Use the locally served face in both scene labels and HTML. Scene texture creation waits for the font to load.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Explicit Inspection Rule",
        "body": "Proximity offers an action; it does not open content or move the visitor automatically.",
        "section": "components"
      }
